<name>Elidir Fawr</name>
<desc>Elidir Fawr is the most northern peak of the Glyderau and means "Big Elidir". It references a warrior king in Welsh legend, Eliffer Gosgorddfawr, who was undefeated in battle. It is also sometimes known as the Electric Mountain, due to the presence of the Dinorwig Power Station inside the mountain, where water flows from the upper reservoir, Marchlyn Mawr, to the lower reservoir, Llyn Peris.</desc>
